@startuml jwt-lifecycle

title JWT Lifecycle — Google ID Token vs Sentinel JWT (CP4)

participant Browser
participant "Google\n(OAuth)" as Google
participant API
database "TimescaleDB\n(users)" as DB

== Phase 1: Google ID Token (short-lived, one-time use) ==

note over Browser, Google
  Issued by Google after OAuth consent flow.
  Proves: "this person authenticated with Google."
  Signed with Google's private keys. Never stored by Sentinel.
end note

Browser -> API : POST /auth/google\n{ id_token: "<google jwt>" }
API -> Google : verifyIdToken() — verify signature\nusing Google's public keys
Google --> API : { sub, email } — identity confirmed
API -> DB : upsert user, get user_id
note right of API
  Google ID token is discarded here.
  It is never stored or forwarded.
end note

== Phase 2: Sentinel JWT (8-hour session token) ==

note over Browser, API
  Issued by the API after Google verification.
  Proves: "this person has an active session in Sentinel."
  Signed with JWT_SECRET (API-owned secret).
  Valid for 8 hours. Stored in HttpOnly cookie.
end note

API -> API : sign JWT\n{ user_id, email, iat, exp: now+8h }\nusing JWT_SECRET
API --> Browser : Set-Cookie: sentinel_jwt=...\nHttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict

== Phase 3: Sentinel JWT used on every request ==

Browser -> API : GET /healthz-auth\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET)\ncheck signature + exp\nextract user_id
note right of API
  No network call.
  No Redis or DB lookup.
  Stateless — local verify only.
end note
API --> Browser : 200 { ok: true, user_id }

== Token expiry ==

note over Browser, API
  After 8 hours: jwt.verify() throws TokenExpiredError → 401.
  If JWT_SECRET rotates: all active cookies become invalid immediately.
end note

@enduml
